Scope
-----

The licence covers all source code in this repository (backend/,
frontend/ and extension/). The label-quality checkpoints are not part of this
repository; the scoring stage downloads the selected one from the
label-quality-assurance release (see below). The licence covers the software
only, not the data produced by running it (collected URLs, detections,
label-quality scores).


Label quality assurance method
------------------------------

The label-quality networks and preprocessing in backend/pipeline/labelqa/
(the unified/, thesis/ and paper/ subpackages) score annotations with the
label quality assurance method. They are copied from the unified/, thesis/
and paper/ folders of the label-quality-assurance repository at commit
07f31da, the maintained implementation of that method with its released
checkpoints and references to its publications:

    https://github.com/piculjantechnologies/label-quality-assurance

The scoring stage downloads the checkpoint that LABELQA_MODEL selects from
the checkpoints released there (unified, the default; thesis; paper):

    https://labelqa.blob.core.windows.net/checkpoints/v1.0/unified__artifacts_voc__best_ema_calibrated.pth
    https://labelqa.blob.core.windows.net/checkpoints/v1.0/thesis__artifacts__best_model_refit.pth
    https://labelqa.blob.core.windows.net/checkpoints/v1.0/paper__artifacts__best_model_refit.pth

That repository, the copied code and the checkpoints are the same author's
work and are licensed AGPL-3.0-only, like Cortex. The checkpoints are
subject to the torchvision BSD 3-Clause notice below, which applies to the
torchvision-derived tensors they contain. See
backend/pipeline/labelqa/MODEL.md.


Third-party components
----------------------

torchvision
    The pipeline uses torchvision model definitions and pretrained
    weights:
    - Object detection runs SSDlite320-MobileNetV3-Large with torchvision's
      COCO-pretrained weights (SSDLite320_MobileNet_V3_Large_Weights),
      which torchvision downloads at run time; they are not redistributed
      here.
    - The label-quality networks are built from torchvision's ResNet-18
      and ResNet-50. Each checkpoint that the scoring stage can download
      has an image trunk that was initialised from torchvision's
      ImageNet-pretrained weights:
      - unified: a ResNet-50 (IMAGENET1K_V2) frozen through layer2 (the
        pretrained parameters, up to weight-EMA floating-point rounding, at
        most 6e-3 absolute), its later stages fine-tuned, so their weights
        are derived from, not copies of, the torchvision parameters;
      - thesis and paper: a ResNet-18 (IMAGENET1K_V1) through layer4,
        fine-tuned, so its weights are derived from, not copies of, the
        torchvision parameters; its BatchNorm running statistics equal the
        pretrained ones up to floating-point rounding (at most 2e-4
        absolute).
      These tensors are subject to the licence below.
    torchvision states that its pretrained models may carry additional
    terms derived from the datasets they were trained on (ImageNet, COCO).

